  "id": "auditory-abilities",
  "term": "auditory abilities",
  "definition": "Auditory abilities are a person’s hearing-related capacities as they experience them in everyday situations, such as following conversations, locating sounds, judging distance, separating simultaneous sounds, and hearing speech or music clearly. In this source, the term refers to perceived performance across these kinds of listening tasks rather than a single skill.",
